# What this backend's rig is, told to bin/test and through it to the suite.
#
# Sourced by bin/test, which exports whatever is assigned here and reads MATRIX_APIS to decide which
# of the suite it can run. Every entry keeps a value which is already set, so one given on the
# command line wins:
#
#   MATRIX_ACCOUNTS=register bin/test

# The APIs this rig serves, which is all five: the homeserver answers the client-server and
# server-server APIs, and docker-compose.yml carries a server for each of the other three, behind a
# profile named for it.
MATRIX_APIS="${MATRIX_APIS:-client-server server-server identity push-gateway application-service}"

# How the suite gets an account. This rig carries a module which registers a user on first login, so
# logging in is enough and registration stays closed.
MATRIX_ACCOUNTS="${MATRIX_ACCOUNTS:-login}"
